WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:04.380
We've heard of suffering for your art, but
some actors take it to extremes.

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:08.180
It's one thing to do your own stunts, but
it's another to completely change your body

00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:10.530
in drastic ways to nail a role.

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:15.230
Some stars eagerly embrace the challenge of
transformation, and still feel the burn after

00:00:15.230 --> 00:00:16.490
the filming stops.

00:00:16.490 --> 00:00:20.679
Here are a few movies that seriously damaged
actors' bodies

00:00:20.679 --> 00:00:23.220
Tom Hardy in The Dark Knight Rises

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:27.310
It's abundantly clear that Tom Hardy isn't
afraid of a little hard work.

00:00:27.310 --> 00:00:32.320
He got into massive shape and broke a few
bones when he played an MMA fighter in Warrior,

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:37.490
and stayed in shape to play Max in Fury Road…
where co-star Charlize Theron accidentally

00:00:37.490 --> 00:00:38.490
broke his nose.

00:00:38.490 --> 00:00:43.500
But it was as everybody's favorite Bane that
he really blew our socks off.

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:45.780
"Bane!!!!!!!"

00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:47.600
….Wait, not that one.

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:48.600
This one.

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:53.090
It was his turn as the beefed-up Bane in the
2012 film The Dark Knight Rises that Hardy

00:00:53.090 --> 00:00:54.530
admits was the hardest.

00:00:54.530 --> 00:00:58.500
Speaking with The Daily Beast, Hardy said
that adding all that muscle weight to his

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:02.070
slight 5'9" frame took a huge a toll, saying,

00:01:02.070 --> 00:01:04.680
"I've probably damaged my body too much.

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:05.680
I'm only little!

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:09.670
If I keep putting on weight I'll collapse
like a house of cards under too much pressure.

00:01:09.670 --> 00:01:12.740
I think you pay the price with any drastic
physical changes.

00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:16.410
It was all right when I was younger, to put
myself under that kind of duress, but I think

00:01:16.410 --> 00:01:20.090
as you get into your 40s you have to be more
mindful."

00:01:20.090 --> 00:01:21.350
Comic accurate?

00:01:21.350 --> 00:01:22.439
Not even close.

00:01:22.439 --> 00:01:25.070
Could still kick our butts inside out?

00:01:25.070 --> 00:01:26.130
Absolutely.

00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:28.610
Matt Damon in Courage Under Fire

00:01:28.610 --> 00:01:33.549
Maybe he felt like he needed to prove himself,
but early in his career, Matt Damon lost 40

00:01:33.549 --> 00:01:38.810
pounds to play a role in the 1996 war drama
Courage Under Fire — and his body came to

00:01:38.810 --> 00:01:40.240
regret it afterwards.

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:43.830
The rapid weight loss caused lasting effects
with his blood sugar.

00:01:43.830 --> 00:01:45.280
Damon told Movieline,

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:50.240
"I ran six miles in the morning and six miles
at night, and I'd drink four to six pots of

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:52.250
coffee to be able to run that distance.

00:01:52.250 --> 00:01:53.820
...I wouldn't waver from my diet.

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:58.170
It got so bad that when my girlfriend kissed
me, I'd have to wash my mouth out because

00:01:58.170 --> 00:02:02.090
I could taste the oils on her lips from the
food she'd eaten."

00:02:02.090 --> 00:02:06.640
Humblebrag about his greasy girlfriend aside,
even director Ed Zwick was shocked at how

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:09.180
thin Damon got, and told him to eat.

00:02:09.180 --> 00:02:13.580
Damon refused, and as a result, Damon had
to remain on medication to moderate his blood

00:02:13.580 --> 00:02:15.270
sugar for a year and a half.

00:02:15.270 --> 00:02:20.080
He clearly learned his lesson: for The Martian,
he simulated his character's severe end-of-movie

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:24.270
weight loss with digital effects instead of
actual starvation.

00:02:24.270 --> 00:02:25.960
Ben Foster in The Program

00:02:25.960 --> 00:02:31.050
Known as a character actor more than a leading
man, Ben Foster shines in just about whatever

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:34.710
he does, and is completely willing to change
his appearance for a role.

00:02:34.710 --> 00:02:39.660
When Foster got the chance to play the disgraced
cyclist Lance Armstrong in the 2015 film The

00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:44.870
Program, he went all in… and that included
taking performance-enhancing drugs as part

00:02:44.870 --> 00:02:46.920
of his research, just like Armstrong.

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:51.140
While Foster maintains that the drugs were
legal and taken under doctor supervision,

00:02:51.140 --> 00:02:56.140
he told the BBC that, unsurprisingly, those
drugs messed with his body for quite awhile

00:02:56.140 --> 00:02:58.220
after the film was wrapped, saying,

00:02:58.220 --> 00:03:02.190
"I had a great doctor, which helped me handle
some of those consequences.

00:03:02.190 --> 00:03:06.271
But it took about half a year to get my levels
right, and I would say for any athlete, you

00:03:06.271 --> 00:03:08.630
have to ask, 'Where are your values?'"

00:03:08.630 --> 00:03:14.650
Reportedly, those values included literally
eating dirt to get a better feel for his character

00:03:14.650 --> 00:03:20.240
in Lone Survivor, and buying, but not taking,
meth for his role in Alpha Dog.

00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:22.410
Gotta draw the line somewhere.

00:03:22.410 --> 00:03:24.650
Matthew McConaughey in Dallas Buyers Club

00:03:24.650 --> 00:03:29.390
Matthew McConaughey has always been known
for his incredible good looks, but these days,

00:03:29.390 --> 00:03:33.790
the actor seems hell-bent on transforming
that handsomeness into something else — and

00:03:33.790 --> 00:03:39.330
it all seemed to start with his Oscar-winning
performance in the 2013 Dallas Buyers Club.

00:03:39.330 --> 00:03:42.730
The then-44-year-old dropped nearly 50 pounds
for the role.

00:03:42.730 --> 00:03:46.460
Describing the experience of losing the weight,
the actor told the BBC,

00:03:46.460 --> 00:03:49.460
"I did it in as healthy a way as I found possible.

00:03:49.460 --> 00:03:50.710
I met with a nutritionist.

00:03:50.710 --> 00:03:53.330
I gave myself four months to lose the weight.

00:03:53.330 --> 00:03:58.280
I had my programmed meals, lost 3.5 pounds
a week — like clockwork — and got down

00:03:58.280 --> 00:04:02.230
to my desired weight, which turned out to
be 47 pounds lighter."

00:04:02.230 --> 00:04:06.460
While McConaughey never mentioned having any
long-lasting problems, it did change him a

00:04:06.460 --> 00:04:08.890
little, because he's never looked quite the
same since.

00:04:08.890 --> 00:04:15.680
See if you even recognize him in 2017's Gold,
for which, among other things, he gained weight.

00:04:15.680 --> 00:04:18.430
Chris Hemsworth in In the Heart of the Sea

00:04:18.430 --> 00:04:23.310
Actor Chris Hemsworth also took the extreme
weight loss plunge for his part in 2015's

00:04:23.310 --> 00:04:27.400
In the Heart of the Sea, where he plays Owen
Chase, a man stranded at sea.

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:31.940
The actor lost 33 pounds to accurately convey
Chase's the suffering, but he admitted it

00:04:31.940 --> 00:04:36.690
took quite a toll on his body and his mind,
more so than building muscle weight for Thor,

00:04:36.690 --> 00:04:38.030
which he told Good Morning America.

00:04:38.030 --> 00:04:42.100
"The gaining is fine, you just eat a lot and
you lift weights but that was underfed, which

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:46.320
led to a pretty moody existence and inconsistent
emotions and so on."

00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:52.100
Hemsworth only ate about 500 calories a day,
consisting of boiled eggs, salads and, quote,

00:04:52.100 --> 00:04:53.190
"nothing much."

00:04:53.190 --> 00:04:55.380
As an actor, Hemsworth wanted to play it real.

00:04:55.380 --> 00:04:58.590
"You know, in order to do it justice - the
story - we had to suffer in some way and we

00:04:58.590 --> 00:04:59.590
did.

00:04:59.590 --> 00:05:01.560
It was, you know, there was not a whole lot
of acting was required."

00:05:01.820 --> 00:05:05.780
Even more impressive, Hemsworth was able to
rebound from the extreme change well enough

00:05:05.790 --> 00:05:09.890
to return to the extremely buff, extremely
Mighty Thor.

00:05:09.890 --> 00:05:11.850
Christian Bale in The Machinist

00:05:11.850 --> 00:05:16.760
If there's a prize for crazy extremes actors
endure for their craft, the award goes to

00:05:16.760 --> 00:05:21.230
Christian Bale, who's known to, uh… really
get into his roles.

00:05:21.230 --> 00:05:24.820
"What the… f--- are you doing?

00:05:24.820 --> 00:05:26.380
Are you professional or not?"

00:05:26.380 --> 00:05:27.380
"Yes, I am"

00:05:27.820 --> 00:05:29.480
" Do I f---ing walk around and rip.."

00:05:29.480 --> 00:05:30.480
NO! Shut the f--- up Bruce!"

00:05:31.120 --> 00:05:34.600
He gained weight for American Hustle, and
bulked up to play Batman.

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:39.340
But it was his turn in the 2004 indie film
The Machinist that became his most infamous

00:05:39.340 --> 00:05:40.340
transformation.

00:05:40.340 --> 00:05:45.270
To play a person suffering from insomnia,
Bale lost 65 pounds by basically eating a

00:05:45.270 --> 00:05:50.810
single can of tuna fish or an apple a day,
along with drinking black coffee and water.

00:05:50.810 --> 00:05:54.950
Even the health professionals he consulted
with warned Bale to not go too far, but he

00:05:54.950 --> 00:05:57.420
ignored their advice, telling Moviepilot,

00:05:57.420 --> 00:06:01.750
"I had been to a nutritionist and when I had
got down to what she had told me was a healthy

00:06:01.750 --> 00:06:03.460
weight, I just went, 'You know what?

00:06:03.460 --> 00:06:04.820
I can go more than this.

00:06:04.820 --> 00:06:05.910
I can keep going.'

00:06:05.910 --> 00:06:10.150
So I lost another 20 pounds below what she
said I should stop at."

00:06:10.150 --> 00:06:13.930
While the transformation was stunning, Bale
explained more of his experience.

00:06:13.930 --> 00:06:17.610
"I didn't actually feel bad until I started
eating again.

00:06:17.610 --> 00:06:21.170
It was when I started putting the weight back
on, that I did it somewhat too rapidly.

00:06:21.170 --> 00:06:26.360
...You know, putting the weight back on I
just wanted to consume pizza and donuts."

00:06:26.360 --> 00:06:30.340
While Bale managed to bounce back, it's a
pretty good bet he won't be taking another

00:06:30.340 --> 00:06:32.870
role as a psycho skeleton in the near future.

00:06:32.870 --> 00:06:36.580
Then again, who wouldn't want to see a movie
called Psycho Skeleton starring Christian

00:06:36.580 --> 00:06:37.580
Bale?

00:06:37.580 --> 00:06:38.590
Answer: no one.

00:06:38.590 --> 00:06:40.300
Thanks for watching!

